# {{ project_name }} CLI

{{ description }}.

`{{ binary_name }}` is a Rust 2024 hook executable generated from
`agent-hook-kit`. It always takes an explicit event subcommand.
{% if harness_mode == "cross" -%}
Cross-harness commands also require an explicit `--harness` value.
{% endif -%}
It never guesses the hook from input JSON.

## Commands

```sh
{% if harness_mode == "cross" -%}
{% for stable_id in aligned_hooks -%}
{{ binary_name }} \
  --harness <{% for selected_harness in harnesses %}{{ "claude" if selected_harness == "claude-code" else selected_harness }}{% if not loop.last %}|{% endif %}{% endfor %}> \
{% if (starter == "immediate_quality" and stable_id == "post_tool") or ((starter == "deferred_quality" or "file_activity" in state_capabilities) and stable_id == "turn_completion") %}  --config <absolute-config-path> \
{% endif %}{% if state_capabilities %}  --state-dir <state-directory> \
{% endif %}  {{ stable_id | replace('_', '-') }}
{% endfor -%}
{% if "file_activity" in state_capabilities %}
{{ binary_name }} \
  --harness <selected-claude-or-codex> \
  --state-dir <state-directory> \
  session-start-state
{% endif -%}
{% else -%}
{% for stable_id in native_hooks -%}
{{ binary_name }} \
{% if "file_activity" in state_capabilities and stable_id == "stop" %}  --config <absolute-config-path> \
{% endif %}{% if state_capabilities %}  --state-dir <state-directory> \
{% endif %}  {{ stable_id | replace('_', '-') }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
```

