{% if state_capabilities %}
All selected state helpers share this package-specific default root, beside
HookKit's per-user default state root:

`$TMPDIR/agent-hook-kit-<uid>/generated/{{ package_name }}/` (Unix)

HookKit creates `agent-hook-kit-<uid>` owner-only, refuses one that another
user owns, and requires every directory from it down to this package's root
to be yours, so users who share a temporary directory cannot tamper with each
other's state, and a directory another user created first fails loudly
instead of being trusted. Use `--state-dir` to override the default, for
example to keep state out of a shared temporary directory altogether. Every
coordinated producer and consumer must receive the same override. A relative
`--state-dir` is resolved against Claude Code's `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`, or the
event's working directory on Codex and Antigravity, by both the generated
state helpers and HookKit's runners, so it names one directory even after the
agent runs `cd`. Persisted family/entity versions are visible in
`src/scaffold/state.rs`.

Every generated event-handler seam receives the parsed state directory as its
fourth argument, including stateless projects. A custom handler can open state
with `scaffold::state::ensure_session_state(context, state_dir)` and then use
any of the selected claims, sets, queues, artifacts, or aggregate helpers. The
stable argument keeps handler edits compatible when state capabilities are
added later.

Library-owned runner commands have no editable event-handler seam. When a
state capability needs custom application logic beyond the runner's coordinated
metadata, file-activity, or artifact work, the questionnaire requires another
selected event with a user-owned handler.
{% endif %}
## Edit policy safely

Files under `src/scaffold/` and the top-level modules in `src/hooks/` are
Copier-owned wiring. Customize the per-event and per-archetype files in the
`src/hooks/aligned/`, `native/`, `pre_tool/`, and `state_types/` directories;
those seams are preserved on recopy, including when selections change. Files
left behind after deselection are harmless and become active again if that
choice is reselected.

Generated files under `config/` are also preserved because they are expected
to become project policy. If you change runner archetype, quality-tool, or
configuration answers later, reconcile the existing Pkl policy manually.

Hook stdout, stderr, and exit status are protocol outputs: do not use
`println!` or uncontrolled `eprintln!` in handlers. Return native decisions
through the generated adapter instead.

## Validate

Run these commands from the generated repository root:

```sh
cargo fmt \
  --manifest-path {{ crate_path }}/Cargo.toml \
  --all -- --check
cargo +{{ compatibility.rust_msrv }} check \
  --manifest-path {{ crate_path }}/Cargo.toml \
  --all-targets
cargo clippy \
  --manifest-path {{ crate_path }}/Cargo.toml \
  --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test \
  --manifest-path {{ crate_path }}/Cargo.toml \
  --all-targets
```

{% if output_mode == "crate" -%}
Copier deliberately did not edit the host `Cargo.toml`. If Cargo reports that
this crate believes it belongs to the surrounding workspace, add this member:

```toml
[workspace]
members = [{{ crate_path | tojson }}]
```

If that workspace still uses `resolver = "2"`, adopt `resolver = "3"` or set
`CARGO_RESOLVER_INCOMPATIBLE_RUST_VERSIONS=fallback`{% if github_actions %}, as
the generated workflow does,{% endif %} so a fresh lockfile keeps the Rust
{{ compatibility.rust_msrv }} check on dependency versions that support it.

This instance uses `.copier-answers.{{ package_name }}.yml`:

```sh
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier update \
  --answers-file .copier-answers.{{ package_name }}.yml .
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier check-update \
  --answers-file .copier-answers.{{ package_name }}.yml \
  --quiet .
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier recopy \
  --answers-file .copier-answers.{{ package_name }}.yml .
```

Before the first copy, verify that `{{ crate_path }}`{% if github_actions %} and
`.github/workflows/{{ package_name }}-hook-ci.yml`{% endif %} are unowned. Do
not use `--overwrite` against an existing repository. A collision means
choosing a different package/path or answering no.
{% else -%}
Update this generated project with:

```sh
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier update .
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier check-update --quiet .
uvx --from copier=={{ compatibility.copier_version }} copier recopy .
```
{% endif %}
Use `update` for normal smart diffing. `recopy` deliberately regenerates the
managed tree from recorded answers and is intended for explicit answer/shape
changes; protected handler seams remain untouched.

After the first successful check, commit the repository's resulting
`Cargo.lock` so the selected HookKit source and transitive dependencies remain
reproducible. Generated CI may use `--locked` after that lockfile exists.

Treat `package_name`, `crate_path`, and `binary_name` as instance identity.
Changing them moves owned files, answers/workflow names, registration commands,
or state namespaces; perform that as an explicit migration or a fresh copy,
not as an ordinary interactive update.

